  <div class="text-block">
    <p>Dear Alumni, Parents, and Friends,</p>
    <p>Travel with us on an exclusive 16-day journey through Patagonia to discover the remarkable diversity of southernmost South America. On this special small group tour, you will visit vibrant cities, explore stunning national parks, and cruise through Southern Patagonia’s spectacular waterways.</p>
    <p>Begin in Buenos Aires with a city tour to explore Palermo’s parks, mansions, and museums, and the colorful bohemian district of La Boca. Attend a tango performance, and also enjoy free time to explore one of the most beautiful and sophisticated cities in the world. Then fly south to Ushuaia, the world’s southernmost urban center, and board the M/V Ventus Australis for a four-night nautical exploration of Southern Chile’s channels and glaciers, ending in Punta Arenas. Experience the jagged peaks, ice-blue glaciers, and turquoise lakes of breathtaking Torres del Paine National Park during a three-night stay. Conclude your journey with two days in the Chilean capital of Santiago, with a visit to a museum and a local winery.</p>
    <p>Space on this exciting program is limited and will fill quickly. Your deposit is fully refundable up until 95 days before departure. Book risk-free today!</p>
    <p>Warmly,</p>
    <p>Cornell Alumni Travel</p>
  </div>

