  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <h2 class="section-title">Patagonian Frontiers</h2>
    <h3 style="text-align: center; font-size: 18pt;">Argentina and Chile by Land & Sea</h3>
    <p class="subtitle" style="font-size: 16pt;">16 days from <span data-field="starting_price_usd">{{ starting_price_usd }}</span> total price from <span data-field="departure_city">{{ departure_city }}</span></p>
    <p class="subtitle" style="font-size: 14pt;">(<span data-field="air_cost_usd">{{ air_cost_usd }}</span> air, land & cruise inclusive plus <span data-field="taxes_fees_usd">{{ taxes_fees_usd }}</span> airline taxes and fees)</p>
  </div>

  <div class="text-block" style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p>Enjoy the rare privilege of face-to-face encounters with two of the world’s last great frontiers: the majestic fjords and glaciers of Southern Patagonia, on a small-ship cruise; and the stunningly dramatic scenery of Torres del Paine on a three-night stay at the park. Along with visits to Buenos Aires and Santiago, we discover the remarkable diversity of South America.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column" style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <div class="column">
      <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px;">Small Group Tour Highlights</h3>
      <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 11pt;">
        <li>Buenos Aires sightseeing • Argentine dinner and tango show</li>
        <li>Four-night cruise through Southern Patagonia channels</li>
        <li>Three-night stay in Torres del Paine with excursions</li>
        <li>Santiago city tour and winery visit</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px;">Day-by-Day Itinerary</h3>
      <table class="table-container">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Day</th>
            <th>Activity</th>
            <th>Rating</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 1</td>
            <td>Depart U.S. for Buenos Aires, Argentina</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 2</td>
            <td>Arrive Buenos Aires after arriving in the lively city this morning, we transfer to our hotel for an afternoon city tour.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 3</td>
            <td>Buenos Aires Highlights of today’s city tour include the lovely mansions and parks of Palermo and the colorful bohemian district of La Boca. Tonight we visit one of the city’s top tango houses for dinner and a performance.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 4</td>
            <td>Buenos Aires today is at leisure.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 5</td>
            <td>Buenos Aires/Ushuaia/Embark Ship We fly today to Ushuaia, Argentina, the world’s southernmost urban center. After lunch on our own time and at leisure in this windswept city, late this afternoon we embark our ship. Early evening we set sail through the Beagle Channel.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 6</td>
            <td>Cruising - Cape Horn/Willy Bay Today we set up one of the world’s last unspoiled from the Beagle Channel to the Drake Passage. We sail through the channels and glaciers, and anchor in the picturesque Willy Bay.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 7</td>
            <td>Cruising - Glacier/Garibaldi Glacier We awaken this morning in Piafjord, home of the stunning glaciers. We take a Zodiac excursion to view the massive glaciers flowing down the mountainside. Later we take inflatable Zodiacs to Agulla Glacier, which we approach via the shore of a lagoon.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 8</td>
            <td>Torres del Paine/Punta Arenas We travel by coach today to Punta Arenas. Upon arrival we transfer to our hotel in the city center.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 9</td>
            <td>Punta Arenas/Santiago We fly today to the Chilean capital, where we enjoy a city tour. Tonight we are dinner guests in the homes of gracious Santiago families.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 10</td>
            <td>Torres del Paine National Park Today we encounter breathtaking Torres del Paine, a 700-square-mile wilderness area. We spend the day exploring this unparalleled landscape of jagged peaks, ice-blue glaciers, turquoise lakes, rushing rivers, and thunderous waterfalls. A highlight: our Zodiac excursion to Agulla Glacier.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 11</td>
            <td>Torres del Paine National Park We see more of Torres del Paine’s pristine wilderness today. Highlights include visits to the crystalline Arnaga Glacier and the glacial waterfall Cascata del Rio Paine. Clear day at Laguna Azul present panoramic vistas of the park’s namesake, the three massive granite Paine Towers. Throughout the day we’re sure to see some of the park’s only permanent residents: 106 species of birds and 26 species of mammals.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 12</td>
            <td>Torres del Paine/Punta Arenas We travel by coach today to Punta Arenas. Upon arrival we transfer to our hotel in the city center.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 13</td>
            <td>Punta Arenas/Santiago We fly today to the Chilean capital, where we enjoy a city tour. Tonight we are dinner guests in the homes of gracious Santiago families.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 14</td>
            <td>Valparaiso Today we encounter the old port of Valparaiso, a one-time fishing village now known as a vibrant cultural hub. We visit a local winery for a private tour and tasting.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 15</td>
            <td>Santiago/Depart for U.S. After a morning at leisure, we enjoy an afternoon visit to the Museum of Pre-Columbian Art, known for its art and artifacts from Chile and across the Americas. From here we transfer to the airport for our overnight flights to the U.S.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Day 16</td>
            <td>Arrive U.S. We arrive in the U.S. this morning and connect with our return flights home.</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
